{
  "source": "dcp-scholarly-authoring/after-A.json",
  "xml": "<response><p id=\"b1\">In this account, <e ref=\"e9\">patronage</e> appears as both <b>opportunity and dependence</b>. <e ref=\"e1\">Leonardo’s</e> move from <e ref=\"e2\">Florence</e> to <e ref=\"e3\">Milan</e> ties artistic work to access to a powerful employer. <e ref=\"e4\">Ludovico’s</e> commission of <e ref=\"e5\">The Last Supper</e> shows a patron helping determine which projects receive support. The mention of <e ref=\"e6\">Cecilia Gallerani</e> broadens the picture of artistic production, although the account does not identify who commissioned her portrait.</p>\n<p id=\"b2\"><mark id=\"s1\" kind=\"claim\">The conquest of <e ref=\"e3\">Milan</e> by <e ref=\"e7\">French forces</e> under <e ref=\"e8\">Louis XII</e> reveals the arrangement’s vulnerability: political upheaval disrupts both <e ref=\"e4\">Ludovico’s</e> court and <e ref=\"e1\">Leonardo’s</e> employment. <e ref=\"e9\">Patronage</e> therefore connects artistic opportunity to political stability; the same concentration of support that enables work can expose an artist’s livelihood to a patron’s changing fortunes.</mark></p>\n<definitions><passage id=\"r1\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Leonardo da Vinci moved from Florence to Milan to work for Ludovico Sforza.\"/>\n<passage id=\"r2\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Ludovico commissioned The Last Supper from Leonardo.\"/>\n<passage id=\"r3\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Leonardo painted Cecilia Gallerani.\"/>\n<passage id=\"r4\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"French forces under Louis XII conquered Milan in 1499, disrupting Ludovico's court and Leonardo's employment.\"/>\n<entity id=\"e1\" name=\"Leonardo da Vinci\" type=\"Person\"><description>Artist identified in the supplied account.</description><alias>Leonardo</alias></entity>\n<entity id=\"e2\" name=\"Florence\" type=\"Place\"><description>Place from which Leonardo moves in the supplied account.</description></entity>\n<entity id=\"e3\" name=\"Milan\" type=\"Place\"><description>Destination of Leonardo's move and location conquered in the supplied account.</description></entity>\n<entity id=\"e4\" name=\"Ludovico Sforza\" type=\"Person\"><description>Leonardo's employer and commissioner of The Last Supper in the supplied account.</description><alias>Ludovico</alias></entity>\n<entity id=\"e5\" name=\"The Last Supper\" type=\"Artwork\"><description>Work commissioned from Leonardo by Ludovico in the supplied account.</description></entity>\n<entity id=\"e6\" name=\"Cecilia Gallerani\" type=\"Person\"><description>Person whom Leonardo painted in the supplied account.</description></entity>\n<entity id=\"e7\" name=\"French forces under Louis XII\" type=\"Military force\"><description>Forces described as conquering Milan in 1499 in the supplied account.</description><alias>French forces</alias></entity>\n<entity id=\"e8\" name=\"Louis XII\" type=\"Person\"><description>Leader under whom the French forces act in the supplied account.</description></entity>\n<entity id=\"e9\" name=\"Artistic patronage\" type=\"Concept\"><description>Support of artistic work through a patron, considered here in relation to opportunity and political dependence.</description><alias>patronage</alias></entity>\n<classify id=\"m1\" target=\"r1\" kind=\"claim\"/>\n<classify id=\"m2\" target=\"r2\" kind=\"claim\"/>\n<classify id=\"m3\" target=\"r3\" kind=\"claim\"/>\n<classify id=\"m4\" target=\"r4\" kind=\"claim\"/>\n<mention id=\"m5\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Leonardo da Vinci\" ref=\"e1\"/>\n<mention id=\"m6\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Florence\" ref=\"e2\"/>\n<mention id=\"m7\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Milan\" prefix=\"from Florence to \" ref=\"e3\"/>\n<mention id=\"m8\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Ludovico Sforza\" ref=\"e4\"/>\n<mention id=\"m9\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Ludovico\" suffix=\" commissioned\" ref=\"e4\"/>\n<mention id=\"m10\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"The Last Supper\" ref=\"e5\"/>\n<mention id=\"m11\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Leonardo\" prefix=\"The Last Supper from \" ref=\"e1\"/>\n<mention id=\"m12\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Leonardo\" suffix=\" painted\" ref=\"e1\"/>\n<mention id=\"m13\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Cecilia Gallerani\" ref=\"e6\"/>\n<mention id=\"m14\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"French forces\" ref=\"e7\"/>\n<mention id=\"m15\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Louis XII\" ref=\"e8\"/>\n<mention id=\"m16\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Milan\" prefix=\"conquered \" ref=\"e3\"/>\n<mention id=\"m17\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Ludovico's\" ref=\"e4\"/>\n<mention id=\"m18\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"Leonardo's\" ref=\"e1\"/>\n<mention id=\"m19\" target=\"@b2aa7818f02_2\" quote=\"patronage\" ref=\"e9\"/>\n<argument id=\"arg1\" target=\"s1\"/>\n<gloss id=\"g1\" target=\"r4\" kind=\"scope\">The relationships recorded here represent the supplied account, not independent historical verification. Its conquest is dated 1499; the interpretation concerns the dependence exposed by the stated disruption, not a claim that all patronage arrangements function identically.</gloss>\n<relation id=\"rel1\" kind=\"entity\" type=\"employed-by\" from=\"e1\" to=\"e4\"/>\n<relation id=\"rel2\" kind=\"entity\" type=\"commissioned\" from=\"e4\" to=\"e5\"/>\n<relation id=\"rel3\" kind=\"entity\" type=\"commissioned-from\" from=\"e5\" to=\"e1\"/>\n<relation id=\"rel4\" kind=\"entity\" type=\"painted\" from=\"e1\" to=\"e6\"/>\n<relation id=\"rel5\" kind=\"entity\" type=\"under-command-of\" from=\"e7\" to=\"e8\"/>\n<relation id=\"rel6\" kind=\"entity\" type=\"conquered\" from=\"e7\" to=\"e3\"/></definitions></response>\n",
